How to Prepare Documents for International Use
Before starting the apostille or translation process, follow a few basic steps.

First, identify the country where the document will be submitted. Next, contact the receiving organization and confirm whether an apostille, legalization, certified translation, or another form of authentication is required.

You should also verify whether the translation must be completed by a specific type of translator or follow a particular certification format.

Make sure that the spelling of names, dates, and other personal information is consistent across all documents. If the receiving authority has provided specific instructions, follow them carefully.

